cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its associated datasets, please cite the PETase Engineering Atlas publication and this software release."
title: "PETase Engineering Atlas"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Vargas Fernández"
    given-names: "Martín Alfredo"
year: 2026
license: MIT
abstract: >
  PETase Engineering Atlas is a group-aware evolutionary framework for
  prioritizing mutation hypotheses in PET hydrolases. The release contains
  the software implementation, frozen evolutionary resources, validation
  outputs, benchmark definitions, reproducibility scripts, and associated
  figure-source data used in the accompanying study.
keywords:
  - PETase
  - PET hydrolase
  - protein engineering
  - enzyme engineering
  - evolutionary bioinformatics
  - mutation prioritization
  - reproducibility
repository-code: "https://github.com/martinvargasfernandez/PETase-Engineering-Atlas"
